# Gemini API key — copy this file to "gemini_api_key.txt" and paste your key below.
#
# Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# Rules of this file:
#   - the FIRST line that is not blank and does not start with # is taken as the key
#   - lines starting with # are comments and are ignored
#   - "gemini_api_key.txt" is gitignored; THIS .example file is not, so never put a
#     real key in it
#
# If no key is found, the bridge keeps using whichever MCP client is connected.
# That is the default and needs no key — a missing key is not an error.
#
# Check which backend is active:
#   python -m host.backend
#
# Alternatives to this file, checked first / last:
#   1. the GEMINI_API_KEY environment variable   (wins over this file)
#   2. this file, in the repo root
#   3. ~/.ai-bridge/gemini_api_key.txt           (if you prefer it outside the repo)
#
# Optional: override the model with the GEMINI_MODEL environment variable.

PASTE_YOUR_KEY_HERE
